//www.dw.com/en/drought-in-germany-and-europe-are-driving-up-costs/a-78447266?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ongoing drought in Europe is causing rivers to dry up and crops to fail. Transport costs are rising and the price of food has exploded. Is inflation due to extreme weather?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why Germany's gas storage levels are so low</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:410c329f739cda1dc0ade31dda3f25c3d933915ca3d9dd932402a6c41a77482b</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-20T14:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-germany-s-gas-storage-levels-are-so-low/a-78440677--5b5bdc8c00df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-germany-s-gas-storage-levels-are-so-low/a-78440677?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's gas storage facilities are only 50% full as traders bet that wholesale prices will fall if the Iran war ends. With around three months until winter, DW asks whether the country can refill its reserves in time.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Munich prosecutors close fatal 1970 antisemitic arson case</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e7fb7f3eaabd40aeaa16d2a642611585923774fb73d905636a98003f5d63f028</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-20T11:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/munich-prosecutors-close-fatal-1970-antisemitic-arson-case/a-78440307--36b64c2972ce.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/munich-prosecutors-close-fatal-1970-antisemitic-arson-case/a-78440307?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prosecutors and police in Munich believe they have identified the man who set a 1970 fire at a Jewish community center and old people's home that killed seven people. But he died in 2020, so prosecution is not possible.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How Europe can better protect against extreme wildfires</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:144b7e0239fd1d7748ef7e2ff91f30350e33b0a91b89c94213d93aebdb74cf6d</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-20T09:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-europe-can-better-protect-against-extreme-wildfires/a-78435243--a1a3032b9e1f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-europe-can-better-protect-against-extreme-wildfires/a-78435243?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In another summer of European wildfires that have even seen wetlands burning, scientists say the situation is set to worsen in the future. What's needed is fire prevention and climate protection.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Bernadette Amani 'living her dream' at Bayern Munich</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2f071ce9a531527e192be5f2ea1b7ba38ef782be1e5da825aa2a1892d457097f</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-20T08:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bernadette-amani-living-her-dream-at-bayern-munich/a-78141213--b6c7f9815814.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bernadette-amani-living-her-dream-at-bayern-munich/a-78141213?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bernadette Amani is heading into her first full season with Bayern Munich, having joined the club in January. Making a living at football is something she never imagined possible while growing up in rural Ivory Coast.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Evergrande founder Hui Ka Yan sentenced to life in prison</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:03d06af47f122ca27ead9918f2ba84aab9dcd597f6db1b549f725639aad0a8ee</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-20T07:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/evergrande-founder-hui-ka-yan-sentenced-to-life-in-prison/a-78439153--ba088f0f4c18.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/evergrande-founder-hui-ka-yan-sentenced-to-life-in-prison/a-78439153?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Chinese court ordered the former billionaire's assets to be confiscated and fined Evergrande-related companies billions of dollars.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Harry and Meghan moving back to Britain: reports</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:136fa4ab041898d292816e56e1f482fc94bdc54c85f470fd8512e7b368e292a5</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-20T03:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/harry-and-meghan-moving-back-to-britain-reports/a-78438052--22486224029e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/harry-and-meghan-moving-back-to-britain-reports/a-78438052?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prince Harry and Meghan Markle will return to the UK after living in the US for over six years, according to reports. The former senior royals will reportedly live in a private residence.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany condemns Israeli minister's Gaza 'killings' remarks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:443b35447e0d2a1bb1c4f56136d1ab109d80b8afa76ed16d1c489b84597cbd69</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-19T16:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-condemns-israeli-minister-s-gaza-killings-remarks/a-78435299--4c019c74804b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-condemns-israeli-minister-s-gaza-killings-remarks/a-78435299?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German Chancellor Friedrich Merz has denounced a call by Israel's far-right security minister to carry out "targeted killings" of Palestinians in Gaza. The outrage spans the entire political spectrum.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Bayern Munich's Jamal Musiala collapses on pitch again</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:953ca6388bec4490c435ce957dd7a2c852aab944af87bbacc0af6dcd2dae7396</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-19T10:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-s-jamal-musiala-collapses-on-pitch-again/a-78426021--80b4bb68cef0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-s-jamal-musiala-collapses-on-pitch-again/a-78426021?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">One of Germany's top footballers has collapsed on the pitch for a second time in four days ahead of the new season. Bayern Munich's Jamal Musiala has said he has a "neurological dysfunction" that causes blackouts.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Minister wants to help renters to install AC</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5da5444fa8498572557a9a6f61fd1028d678aabc7ad8fec907341a179219981b</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-19T09:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-minister-wants-to-help-renters-to-install-ac/live-78421815--8a3f5e5a2022.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-minister-wants-to-help-renters-to-install-ac/live-78421815?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The justice minister wants to make it easier for tenants to install air conditioning or external blinds. Meanwhile, a defense CEO is reportedly in hiding after being warned of Russian plots to kill him.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Who really owns the Caspian Sea?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0018a1f5a35cb31af6619a4de28736fd7e39035129018d43c4427e34cdc7da01</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-19T09:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/who-really-owns-the-caspian-sea/a-78396946--815c4887a22c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/who-really-owns-the-caspian-sea/a-78396946?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Five countries border the Caspian Sea, but none owns a fixed share. A 2018 convention established rules for navigation, security and fishing while leaving some seabed borders unresolved.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Messi retirement hint highlights football era nearing an end</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:36a71484874259e7dddb2191881de86ed02718d4e511757ab6a5aef5007f6ce7</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-19T08:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/messi-retirement-hint-highlights-football-era-nearing-an-end/a-78415527--f2918eb8eee5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/messi-retirement-hint-highlights-football-era-nearing-an-end/a-78415527?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Soon after propelling Argentina to a second consecutive World Cup final, Lionel Messi has cast some doubt on his future. While retirement doesn't seem imminent, it still beckons for him and Cristiano Ronaldo.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>In drought-stricken France, tankers supply drinking water</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:15c90cb406b621946b812ace10f1c4194a9bc9d9921665cd362c7e2e5f1e4fe9</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-19T04:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/in-drought-stricken-france-tankers-supply-drinking-water/a-78420016--bd4077809bc7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/in-drought-stricken-france-tankers-supply-drinking-water/a-78420016?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">France is seeing water shortages in regions that usually have plenty of supply. This summer's extreme heat is exposing how unprepared much of the country, and Europe, is for increasing water scarcity.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Will Germany's drought push up food prices?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:87351e693eff170c4e32df490e3abb4d7a3dd46ce2e81064e16e3fe9e3ce5599</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-18T14:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-germany-s-drought-push-up-food-prices/a-78408203--1f8c5e8778fa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-germany-s-drought-push-up-food-prices/a-78408203?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's main farmers' association has warned of a below-average harvest after drought and crops damaged by extreme heat. DW looks into what lower yields could mean for food prices and grocery bills.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Dressed for power: Giorgia Meloni and the language of fashion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:504f810162d86b221974c01def865ef8729095cf79df34825c9a695de11c7a74</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-18T14:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dressed-for-power-giorgia-meloni-and-the-language-of-fashion/a-78413559--c708abdeeebc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dressed-for-power-giorgia-meloni-and-the-language-of-fashion/a-78413559?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From Giorgia Meloni's shift from dark suits to pastels to Angela Merkel's signature jackets, politicians have long used clothing to shape how voters see them. In this day and age, power dressing has evolved.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>How to grow food for more people in a hotter world</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:50f32171e261efab0fb5d0c3d7d95fe7d4996f5e63cce7ed51ed8db1f3f76b98</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-18T13:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-to-grow-food-for-more-people-in-a-hotter-world/a-78413324--6e9042895db0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-to-grow-food-for-more-people-in-a-hotter-world/a-78413324?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Inside futuristic labs, plants are scanned, stressed and analyzed. The aim is to use the results to produce plant strains that can better serve a growing population in a warming world.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>How Germany's Hyrox became a global fitness craze</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:14c0dacbe620d6a3eda472ab4b19bac4ea5dd2adb66db44dc4bb15bc2f3ddcd7</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-18T09:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-germany-s-hyrox-became-a-global-fitness-craze/a-78074218--d75cba260312.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-germany-s-hyrox-became-a-global-fitness-craze/a-78074218?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Created in Germany and now a global success, Hyrox combines running and functional training into a unique format. How a German concept became an international sports phenomenon.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Do not inhale! How wildfire smoke 'affects the whole body'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6e8dc852957d496ce7d2533246b4e1e2bbdfcd13be0c9be3419b3b5a1e455cb3</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-18T08:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/do-not-inhale-how-wildfire-smoke-affects-the-whole-body/a-76039654--04a98638c5fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/do-not-inhale-how-wildfire-smoke-affects-the-whole-body/a-76039654?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Wildfires destroy lives and livelihoods. But survivors and firefighters also suffer long-term harm to their health. A growing body of research suggests particulate matter (PM2.5) in wildfire smoke is a major culprit.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Bundeswehr troop numbers reach 13-year high</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fca861a08c381ab952eff612f3c5b57e04416bd03c763e23b2b53a75fe964442</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-17T15:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-bundeswehr-troop-numbers-reach-13-year-high/a-78400706--342d0fde0e74.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-bundeswehr-troop-numbers-reach-13-year-high/a-78400706?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's Defense Ministry is reporting a comparatively rare success story in its bid to bolster troop numbers. At the end of July, the total stood at around 186,700, roughly 3,700 more than a year earlier — a 2% boost.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Norway wealth fund sounds alarm on AI stock market bubble</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6026d8199fc6eeacb4a32921219ec2b1a54082eb707b398f6d733b750fc1d679</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-17T14:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/norway-wealth-fund-sounds-alarm-on-ai-stock-market-bubble/a-78351371--685600a6d47d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/norway-wealth-fund-sounds-alarm-on-ai-stock-market-bubble/a-78351371?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The head of Norway's sovereign wealth fund has warned that soaring AI-driven stock valuations could trigger a sharp correction. How exposed is the world's largest sovereign wealth fund to a market downturn?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Can the cool north handle a surge in climate tourism?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:48d7f60f9b546d3573973740e52ea0275597cb1a37278e68b820d79a1c8f3541</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-17T11:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-the-cool-north-handle-a-surge-in-climate-tourism/a-78362462--18cb3d6fa134.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-the-cool-north-handle-a-surge-in-climate-tourism/a-78362462?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With heat records continually being broken and southern summers getting hotter, travelers are heading north. Fragile ecosystems are paying the price.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's AfD is labeled far right, populist or extremist</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:979e57987e7d3d5eb7e8b6c1200e4fb06d6bebcdab0ac6efee8578543ae73e0d</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-17T10:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-afd-is-labeled-far-right-populist-or-extremist/a-78395043--6d6a7c2a5b04.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-afd-is-labeled-far-right-populist-or-extremist/a-78395043?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Right wing, far right, fascist: Many terms are being thrown around in the debate about the AfD. What do they mean, and how appropriate are they when discussing the AfD? DW has a glossary.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Fatty food raises risk of colorectal cancer</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:688519c6925a55649d89dccf9a4c7f4c74ad5636207a89133015956ee0b0e6f3</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-17T06:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fatty-food-raises-risk-of-colorectal-cancer/a-78284704--78a75758e125.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fatty-food-raises-risk-of-colorectal-cancer/a-78284704?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Did you know fatty foods can increase production of an acid in your gut that promotes tumor growth? That's on top of all the other health risks linked to fatty foods, like fries and burgers.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Belgium blaze kept out of Germany for now</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:21a1fcb84c2142acb206a5cfb11b902e4c6950bf314727b87aed0e8cb64b16b5</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-17T06:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-belgium-blaze-kept-out-of-germany-for-now/live-78391144--2aa38b52aa2e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-belgium-blaze-kept-out-of-germany-for-now/live-78391144?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Some residents in the Eifel town of Monschau were evacuated as a massive fire in Belgium threatened to cross the border. Meanwhile, shipping shortfalls amid low river water levels could hit the construction industry.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How Germany supports recovery of Berlin Pride attack victims</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f28695935f28e2c6ef9b4225fa512d1ac0e8e7eb60f60148fa79e911f9770bf0</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-16T05:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-germany-supports-recovery-of-berlin-pride-attack-victims/a-78370256--a1aa505254e7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-germany-supports-recovery-of-berlin-pride-attack-victims/a-78370256?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After a terrorist attack, public attention tends to focus primarily on the perpetrator. But what about the victims? What support can they expect? And what lies ahead for them?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>In Germany, record heat meets climate action fatigue</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7803007786f699547a4500aff6b1191ceeadb77b18a65b1a9ba983e926b54d7d</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-15T14:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/in-germany-record-heat-meets-climate-action-fatigue/a-78374727--137871110abb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/in-germany-record-heat-meets-climate-action-fatigue/a-78374727?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Climate action does not seem to be a priority for the German government — despite record temperatures, heat-related deaths and drought. Why aren't more people taking to the streets in protest?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Afghan allies still waiting for the safety Germany promised</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ba745cc0f1d2a457bb424dd5b29c106da5f857c6922049bca7e7f30a88a44af2</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-15T11:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/afghan-allies-still-waiting-for-the-safety-germany-promised/a-78319745--eaebff6d37be.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/afghan-allies-still-waiting-for-the-safety-germany-promised/a-78319745?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After the Taliban retook power on August 15, 2021, Berlin promised to bring Afghan staff to Germany. But people are still waiting to leave in Pakistan and Afghanistan.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Evacuated villagers return after Eifel wildfire eases</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0767b2a521808c57086c3d14684b987ec0d1e841e6448f5be827846bcd8f2be5</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-15T07:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-evacuated-villagers-return-after-eifel-wildfire-eases/live-78378773--98a57d61b602.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-evacuated-villagers-return-after-eifel-wildfire-eases/live-78378773?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Most residents evacuated from the village of Gey have returned home after firefighters brought a major wildfire in Germany's Eifel region largely under control. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Berlin's Russian House: A hub for propaganda and espionage?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:16ca6cf63c22c43c4e13d161a004976fb868f0247ebcfaf89f33f59f495c082c</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-14T10:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/berlin-s-russian-house-a-hub-for-propaganda-and-espionage/a-73037945--1262294c273c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/berlin-s-russian-house-a-hub-for-propaganda-and-espionage/a-73037945?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Russian House stands in the heart of Berlin. Critics have long said it's being used to spread propaganda for Putin's Russia. Now, French authorities have said it is being used by the Kremlin for espionage.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Why women are breaking men's endurance records</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:18a9daee6908a3508641581c228b7de8544106991876404b09a245b05512b101</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-14T09:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-women-are-breaking-men-s-endurance-records/a-78362321--f787f66106e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-women-are-breaking-men-s-endurance-records/a-78362321?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Sophie Woods has completed the 2,000-kilometer Via Alpina faster even than the fastest-ever man. DW explains why she is not the only woman breaking men's records in extreme sports.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Hunger stones: The history behind 'if you see me, weep'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b5c6fc36402db775377a825eb2a27788801675068cfbc3dfb6ef3baa82319361</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-14T07:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hunger-stones-the-history-behind-if-you-see-me-weep/a-78345729--34d8ccc8292a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hunger-stones-the-history-behind-if-you-see-me-weep/a-78345729?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Centuries-old hunger stones are emerging as Europe's rivers recede. Among the most famous is the Decin hunger stone in the Elbe River with its cryptic message.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Can a drug help prevent trauma? Study with mice suggests so</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:23612ea3e45ca648e06525b5ead625e261a6237867ca18cad0030b7749b77d10</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-14T06:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-a-drug-help-prevent-trauma-study-with-mice-suggests-so/a-78301961--0a25b16be584.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-a-drug-help-prevent-trauma-study-with-mice-suggests-so/a-78301961?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Researchers in Munich and Stockholm blocked the lifelong social cost of early adversity in mice with a single compound. The catch: it only worked when given during the trauma, not after.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Can we go green without forever chemicals?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c83de73a86fb2e41db851db17b2aa13cfd6b3f8c047fda129b5d8559124d631e</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-13T07:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-we-go-green-without-forever-chemicals/a-77888704--5cf595a2a5e7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-we-go-green-without-forever-chemicals/a-77888704?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As nations globally move to ban forever chemicals, should renewable energy technologies be exempt for the sake of saving the climate?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Eurovision bars countries at war from hosting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae5b0dfcb470fd9d3cf9df89ea590f9477a69a0c89a659463331c1445416b4b4</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-12T18:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eurovision-bars-countries-at-war-from-hosting/a-78341915--0c283d70de4e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eurovision-bars-countries-at-war-from-hosting/a-78341915?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Eurovision victory will no longer guarantee hosting rights if war or a wider security crisis affects the winning country. The change could have particular significance for recent high-flyers Ukraine and Israel.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Mozart tribute ends on sour note after mass figurine theft</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5027193c603cefa7d9971f733cf9c36c7e28c5f4472ad4daee895e83f41d62f0</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-12T16:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mozart-tribute-ends-on-sour-note-after-mass-figurine-theft/a-78341647--5357f5e2d579.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mozart-tribute-ends-on-sour-note-after-mass-figurine-theft/a-78341647?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A playful tribute to Mozart has turned into a whodunit after 210 gold-colored figures disappeared from one of Austria's busiest tourist spots. The mass theft forced organizers to end the outdoor display early.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU waste packaging rules: Why small businesses are worried</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da939a0ce72469ecf7db7062733779a3b2a59961d08108d21a75d08307af021a</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-12T09:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-waste-packaging-rules-why-small-businesses-are-worried/a-78326555--4758d7b19395.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-waste-packaging-rules-why-small-businesses-are-worried/a-78326555?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU has introduced new rules targeting packaging waste and "forever chemicals." Although the changes will be phased in slowly, some small sellers have already paused shipments due to the additional red tape.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>AI helping create popular mobile sports games</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:913874cb71dc601178afeb77fd6628ad44ed8f4de08dfca37216c99ef441c6e6</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-12T09:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ai-helping-create-popular-mobile-sports-games/a-78229226--c5ddee08c15c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ai-helping-create-popular-mobile-sports-games/a-78229226?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After the World Cup and before the domestic season, many fans still crave more football. Amateur coders are helping to fill this gap.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Solar eclipse: What to look forward to</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c4174990a9a574a9dee46419b31835f220e5db5cf25db98eba7eb3d14f88061e</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-12T07:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/solar-eclipse-what-to-look-forward-to/a-78330594--591cb72e69ae.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/solar-eclipse-what-to-look-forward-to/a-78330594?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The last solar eclipse visible from the European mainland was in 1999. Here's what to expect, and how to prepare for this rare occasion.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Making sense of Trump's executive order on US vaccinations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f5b310befe228c2aa924eda73722c3b7d66d73aa6fd74fdd7cf6c05e1765b51</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-11T15:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/making-sense-of-trump-s-executive-order-on-us-vaccinations/a-78321723--93af87101bd5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/making-sense-of-trump-s-executive-order-on-us-vaccinations/a-78321723?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump and his Health Secretary Robert F. Kennedy Jr. have long tried to reduce the number of vaccinations available to the US public and even farm animals. The latest move in context.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>How one German city plans to challenge climate extremes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:156bbe983a6590f9935dc5810c862aea05e5786fb0f413c9fbcd60f83d36c320</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-11T07:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-one-german-city-plans-to-challenge-climate-extremes/a-78278373--b05b98bfdb8c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-one-german-city-plans-to-challenge-climate-extremes/a-78278373?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Western Europe has recorded its hottest-ever June and July, and extreme weather from drought to storms is here to stay. How can we adapt to a fundamentally altered climate? Cities like Kiel are trying new ideas.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>How the Rhine drought threatens Germany's economic recovery</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c4d0e26b867590a73a5326c1ad01eed9cc856aa3b3c88ba968000f9f575f9b22</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-10T15:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-the-rhine-drought-threatens-germany-s-economic-recovery/a-78300076--3aa1de887ea7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-the-rhine-drought-threatens-germany-s-economic-recovery/a-78300076?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's inland waterways still move around 5% of the nation's goods. With the Rhine at a critically low level, DW explores how the drought is hitting the economy where it hurts most.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>UEFA, other football federations unite against Infantino</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a806540b0ac8e46af33a3c94621477b2592f5f4a487076c272c6118312a306d2</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-10T11:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uefa-other-football-federations-unite-against-infantino/a-78301601--e313c442a148.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uefa-other-football-federations-unite-against-infantino/a-78301601?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A few weeks ago, Gianni Infantino looked set for another unopposed term as FIFA president. Now, with an election looming, the beleagured football executive is counting the numbers and could be hanging by a thread.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Type 2 diabetes in young women increasingly common</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1b52e14f73bdccbe4252b2e442cd33015fb65d5985068cc8c7c594523fdb048c</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-10T06:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/type-2-diabetes-in-young-women-increasingly-common/a-78251712--f4920d55bd53.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/type-2-diabetes-in-young-women-increasingly-common/a-78251712?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">British researchers say rates of type 2 diabetes are growing most among women under 40. The disease is often underdiagnosed in women or diagnosed too late to reverse the condition's progression.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Study: Obesity 'bigger cancer risk' than previously thought</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f265c43a2f33347f51536616f13d09c464434bdaf60e8ace8d822f9c69f8ab52</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-09T09:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/study-obesity-bigger-cancer-risk-than-previously-thought/a-78291063--3902cce5a489.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/study-obesity-bigger-cancer-risk-than-previously-thought/a-78291063?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new study has found that being significantly overweight could be responsible for more cases of cancer than previously known. Abdominal fat, in particular, increases the risk of cancer — especially among women.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>FIFA warns against 'concerted effort' to undermine Gianni Infantino</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:192e09068e22ecf793cb6d0f3152087c60f962d54159cdcd3b7e3373e91b6b9a</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-09T00:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fifa-warns-against-concerted-effort-to-undermine-gianni-infantino/a-78291551--590c09705a5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fifa-warns-against-concerted-effort-to-undermine-gianni-infantino/a-78291551?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Pressure is mounting on the FIFA president Gianni Infantino after plans to sell a stake in the World Cup collapsed and fresh allegations emerged relating to his time at UEFA.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Eco wins: Hungary goes solar, marmots go viral and Rome gets an upgrade</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9dd7cc9f54911e2e01af157e008f186b22764e4949ceb3a58b707b21bb091cb6</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-07T14:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eco-wins-hungary-goes-solar-marmots-go-viral-and-rome-gets-an-upgrade/a-78281783--5797de72a6fb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eco-wins-hungary-goes-solar-marmots-go-viral-and-rome-gets-an-upgrade/a-78281783?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From Hungary's accidental solar revolution to marmot crowdfunding and a long-overdue upgrade for Rome's big snake, good news comes in strange packages this week.</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>Testosterone and fertility: the trade-off men aren't told about</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d6457644ec4214aa5a1006cef4bb8c8ca3a334931cba3ced91bd76d419ca4dc3</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-07T08:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/testosterone-and-fertility-the-trade-off-men-aren-t-told-about/a-78216799--15f9b1938148.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/testosterone-and-fertility-the-trade-off-men-aren-t-told-about/a-78216799?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Testosterone is trending in gyms, on social online and in politics. US Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth even wants troops screened for low testosterone. But taking supplements can shut down the body's natural production.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Drought threatens power supplies in Danube countries</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4ac522de8ce44a79d578764a83e2268c6f1fb90042a935805cd33a4586d38e66</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-06T19:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/drought-threatens-power-supplies-in-danube-countries/a-78269916--13a83dfe0a9a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/drought-threatens-power-supplies-in-danube-countries/a-78269916?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Droughts, heat and falling water levels in the Danube are hitting central and southeastern Europe hard. Hungary and Romania are experiencing an energy crisis — whereas countries like Bulgaria are better prepared.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Mata Hari: Celebrated dancer turns WWI spy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b3b56974a60cd4164e537fc2de900fb2803bcae37ae2cf35701437350c1bfc9a</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-06T14:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mata-hari-celebrated-dancer-turns-wwi-spy/a-78263857--aeacf364a625.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mata-hari-celebrated-dancer-turns-wwi-spy/a-78263857?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Mata Hari enthralled Europe's elite with her beauty and performances. Accused of spying during World War I, she faced a French firing squad in 1917.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>AfD threatens to cut funding for 'modern-thinking' culture</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ac9647cbbfd4c0807299ce2e5466385847decec522c0a8f8e6ab577630065a8</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-06T13:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/afd-threatens-to-cut-funding-for-modern-thinking-culture/a-78071511--85e5e256bec6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/afd-threatens-to-cut-funding-for-modern-thinking-culture/a-78071511?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The far-right party could win an absolute majority in Saxony-Anhalt's state election in September. Their cultural program denigrates Bauhaus, Holocaust remembrance culture and diversity in theater.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>How Gianni Infantino rose to rule football</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:31519d81313e0c8892a0b5a3ca809a94524c27f07c1643630f59f11909322b81</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-06T12:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-gianni-infantino-rose-to-rule-football/a-78242568--673de12a0671.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-gianni-infantino-rose-to-rule-football/a-78242568?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Gianni Infantino is staying on as FIFA president despite growing pressure to step down. So who is football's most powerful man, why did UEFA and others turn against him, and how did he reassert his authority?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Why is Russia selling its gold?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b019a601c6fedf816b00a74bbe0221de2b76804bb4c83c68d8c34404e27bdb6d</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-06T08:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-is-russia-selling-its-gold/a-78145069--271482f77eda.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-is-russia-selling-its-gold/a-78145069?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia has become one of the world's biggest sellers of gold over the past 12 months. It's an attempt to raise cash in the face of budget issues, but not necessarily a sign of a looming financial crisis.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>The hidden problem with small modular nuclear reactors</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:347d1a5c490f13230ff5756b9033f448edcb5b1cfce2e3d211a9adacaea220aa</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-05T12:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-hidden-problem-with-small-modular-nuclear-reactors/a-77491854--fae84071e0d1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-hidden-problem-with-small-modular-nuclear-reactors/a-77491854?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Mini nuclear reactors are seen as a flexible energy source. Their promise: abundant energy, cheap, clean and climate-friendly with lower water use. But do the numbers add up? We look at what's behind the SMR hype.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>My sleep deprivation is your natural short sleep</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2fafb841707dd23066aaba32100fd107106d8e3255f324d4dd41ed62af356281</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-05T12:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/my-sleep-deprivation-is-your-natural-short-sleep/a-78247228--462679867791.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/my-sleep-deprivation-is-your-natural-short-sleep/a-78247228?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Every so often we hear of high-ranking politicians or CEOs claiming to get by on very little sleep — some as little as three hours a night. If they're not natural short sleepers, chances are they're heading for trouble.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>AI ecosystem's 'circular' investment: risk or advantage?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:85b30cec28e28f781bda697bb0690abb25ea7e1bd3a3ccbcfaf3779f4f177004</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-05T06:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ai-ecosystem-s-circular-investment-risk-or-advantage/a-78186917--3b32948195fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ai-ecosystem-s-circular-investment-risk-or-advantage/a-78186917?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Amid talk of an AI sector bubble, one aspect is under scrutiny. Many big AI players are invested in smaller ones, who then buy the bigger firm's products. This brings risks and advantages.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>South Sudan: How climate change can result in toxic water</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:97607db846f78685edb289969bc34a8c571f59dfd8fd47809fe3137e82f32a7d</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-04T14:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-sudan-how-climate-change-can-result-in-toxic-water/a-78193418--3cc7d4e2a52a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-sudan-how-climate-change-can-result-in-toxic-water/a-78193418?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Years of flooding have resulted in disastrous water pollution in South Sudan's main oil region. As communities, scientists and health workers scramble for solutions, the long-term impacts of the crisis is yet to emerge.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Tennis star Sabalenka supports sport's new sex test policy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cca759d268d6fdf9e41fac2f5f76d16bdcd0510fada39ffff94c0d46539e6383</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-04T11:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tennis-star-sabalenka-supports-sport-s-new-sex-test-policy/a-78228069--9bec58810e3b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tennis-star-sabalenka-supports-sport-s-new-sex-test-policy/a-78228069?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The world number one women's tennis player supports the WTA's new sex testing rules. Others are more critical of the policy.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>More cancer-prone? Why younger generations may be at risk</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9d9148560263b7c8812a14b358660407c675be8c25f76a2404d242f087d5d316</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-03T18:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/more-cancer-prone-why-younger-generations-may-be-at-risk/a-78163655--f7ca34b315d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/more-cancer-prone-why-younger-generations-may-be-at-risk/a-78163655?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Researchers are observing certain age-related types of cancer more frequently in younger people. A new study suggests this could be because younger generations are aging faster than their parents or grandparents.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Binging on cringe: It's as addictive as 'eating junk food'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a4d9d561035a0d23014484d26c2905bb5a9cc133f0f3ebe6cee058c5cb7db512</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-03T14:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/binging-on-cringe-it-s-as-addictive-as-eating-junk-food/a-78145287--3dd804438c34.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/binging-on-cringe-it-s-as-addictive-as-eating-junk-food/a-78145287?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Flexing achievements? Cringe. Expressing genuine emotions? Cringe. You want to look away, but you can’t. Cringe. It's so addictive, people have built social media careers by monetizing other people's worst moments.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>What happens next for Infantino and FIFA?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe19e537db8f4dd0d8f39bff78d7558f613aa293fa0e857f067a3b989d67b419</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-03T10:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-happens-next-for-infantino-and-fifa/a-78213350--fd7b887fe2e0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-happens-next-for-infantino-and-fifa/a-78213350?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">FIFA President Gianni Infantino is under pressure after the failure of his plan to create a commercial subsidiary for the World Cup. But will he be ousted? And what is needed for that to happen?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>The economic toll of Spain's wildfires</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cfcbfa76a4623de04debf38c7e85deb7ffc4d77d9692e0faa39194f70665ed6c</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-03T05:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-economic-toll-of-spain-s-wildfires/a-78186441--47a78e5edc78.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-economic-toll-of-spain-s-wildfires/a-78186441?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Devastating wildfires are ravaging Spain's tourism, economy and nature. Could the country have done more to prevent them?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: As temperatures rise, so does climate skepticism</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:18ec9c3c0d16b3945c37fac4790a63a2cecd30cfb5e06b6847ca18dabc3e6817</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-02T08:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-as-temperatures-rise-so-does-climate-skepticism/a-78206354--f4057537ed76.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-as-temperatures-rise-so-does-climate-skepticism/a-78206354?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Some 98% of active climate scientists say climate change is happening, and is man-made. Nonetheless, a new study shows the number of climate-change skeptics in Germany has increased. Why is that?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>More women die in heatwaves, but biology 'isn't main cause'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c7bb524fe0171c9ab0d63e08e040e174b683b27b800822b9b71f65792cdd67a9</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-01T11:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/more-women-die-in-heatwaves-but-biology-isn-t-main-cause/a-78187451--c76d763c9f42.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/more-women-die-in-heatwaves-but-biology-isn-t-main-cause/a-78187451?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In country after country, more women are dying from the heat than men. But researchers say biology isn't the main reason. Age, working conditions, and unequal access to rest may drive the gap.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry></feed>
